  "displayName": "Saltings Reach",
  "notes": [
    "Saltings Reach (#12, #36): the tidal estuary, the v1.0 current venue (#11). The reach runs east from the sea between a sea-walled north bank and reed beds on the south bank, with a headland on the south bank.",
    "Venue frame: metres, x east, y north. Directions are compass bearings in degrees. Schema: docs/venue-file.md.",
    "The channel meanders along the middle of the reach, about 8 m deep at its deepest; mudflats shoal to the north bank and a narrower shelf to the south. Peak 2 kn in the channel (#14 keeps the estuary's 2 kn peak); the flood runs east, up the reach, and the ebb west. A headland eddy forms downstream of the south-bank point.",
    "Classic oscillating: from the west-south-west, down the reach from the sea, so the course runs along the channel: the flood runs down the course, the ebb up it. Gusty offshore: from the north-north-west, off the north bank, so the course crosses the channel.",
    "Geographic grids, one per pairing (#10): shadow of up to 24 % in the lee of the banks and up to 4 deg of bend near them; over the race areas within 5 % and 2 deg. The current is this venue's puzzle, not the wind.",
    "Any tide state at the gun. Checked offline (#83): the longest beat's race area at every seeded rotation (+-10 deg) stays clear of land and inside both grids, holds channel and shallows, and is sailable in a 25 % lull at peak tide."
  ],
